description:
Treasury is the centralized function of the company to manage the liquidity and capital positions, ensuring sufficient resources to support business growth and optimizing the use of the balance sheet by minimize idle cash and optimize investment return. Reporting to the Financial Controller, you will be a core member of the team, duties include, but not limited to:










 Responsibilities










 • Execute daily fund transfers, monitor cash balances, and conduct regular bank account maintenance.




 • Support funding note issuance, including issuance documents preparation, data analysis, size management etc.




 • Maintain banking relationships, including post\-loan management, credit line negotiations, pricing discussions, and deposit management etc.




 • Prepare daily and monthly reports for management review.




 • Support to define the requirements on system solution and system testing.




 • Support other ad\-hoc tasks and team initiatives.






















 Requirements










 • Master Degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, or a related field;




 • Team player with unquestionable integrity and ethical standards;




 • Self\-starter with willingness to learn and contribute;




 • Strong in logical reasoning, good sense to numbers;




 • Independent and critical thinking skills and strong financial acumen;




 • Good English and Mandarin ability, both in speaking and writing;




 • Good verbal and written communication skills (must including Chinese) and with ability to articulate effectively ideas and technical concepts to non\-technical audiences.

Within Natixis CIB, Global Markets brings together trading, structuring, and sales of financial instruments expertise (structured products, derivatives, forward and spot instruments) offering both hedging and investments solutions to a wide range of clients, including corporates, financial institutions, insurance companies, etc.




 Within Global Markets, we offer a complete range of expertise across all assets such as rates, credit, foreign exchange, equities, and commodities.










 Operating in 30 countries, Natixis CIB delivers expertise across all major financial hubs, including Europe, Asia Pacific \& the Middle East (APME), and the Americas.




 Designed to accelerate both professional and personal growth, the International Global Markets Talent Pool at Natixis CIB will give you access to a tailored learning journey across different departments, enabling you to gain confidence and autonomy quickly and make an impact from day one.










 If you have recently graduated, then the International Global Markets Talent Pool offers a unique opportunity to build strong foundations for your career while exploring a diverse, challenging and fast\-paced environment.










**On a daily basis, your main responsibilities will be to:** 



* Grow as part of a team of multidisciplinary experts: Trading, Structuring, Sales, Syndication, Quantitative Analysts, etc;
* Gain exposure to global markets through a variety of assignments across our diverse departments and locations;
* Keep yourself updated on crucial economic and financial information that could impact our clients and the products we offer;
* Work and evolve in an international, multicultural and energetic environment;
* Develop your skills through a tailor\-made program.









 You will work in an international environment, within a community of experts that values collaboration, excellence, continuous learning and collective actions.




 This position is open worldwide. International mobility between plateforms may be offered based on business needs, individual preferences and applicable administrative requirements (including visa, work authorisation eligibility, etc.) across our US, APAC and EMEA office locations.








**Profile :** 










 This position is open to recent graduates, or those who will graduate this Summer, with the following profile:



* Excellent academic background in Engineering, Finance, Economics or Mathematics;
* Experience or internship within investment banking or related field;
* Good understanding of the investment banking environment and global markets;
* Fluency in written and spoken English.
* Furthermore, programming skills and the ability to use VBA or Python would be an asset, as well as international experience as part of your studies or internship.









 With excellent interpersonal skills and a strong ability to foster innovation, you also demonstrate:



* Dynamism, proactivity and curiosity;
* Team spirit, collaboration and initiative;
* A results\-driven and client\-focused mindset;
* Excellent communication skills with a proactive attitude and willingness to learn and develop.















 Asia Pacific Applicants please kindly apply:










 Analyst \- Talent Pool \- Global Market \- External Site Careers

