The West Kowloon Cultural District Authority welcomes exceptional talent with a passion to realise the vision and mission of making the West Kowloon Cultural District a prime local and international destination for arts, culture and entertainment.




**You Will Be Responsible For**
* partnering with business stakeholders to identify and prioritise analytics opportunities supporting institutional objectives;
* delivering end\-to\-end execution of analytics initiatives, from scoping and stakeholder interviews to deployment and performance measurements;
* supporting the design and development of a unified business datasets and analytics framework (e.g. GA4\) through integration with multiple data sources across WKCD;
* analysing large and complex business datasets to identify patterns, trends and actionable insights on user behaviours, process performance and market dynamics;
* presenting findings and recommendations in clear, accessible language to business stakeholders and decision\-makers;
* working with IT and data engineering to implement; and
* performing any other duties from time to time as reasonably assigned by the Authority.


**You Should**
* possess a Bachelor's degree in data science, statistics, mathematics, or a related field;
* have 6\+ years of relevant experience in data analytics and analytics frameworks in a complex organisational setting;
* have hands\-on experience with GA4, data warehousing solutions and BI tools (e.g. Tableau, Power BI);
* have Expert\-level SQL skills. Google Analytics Certified, Google Data Analytics Professional Certificate, or Microsoft Power BI Certification are strong plus;
* have deep experience with Google Analytics 4 and its BigQuery integration. Experience with Python or R for advanced analytics is a plus; and
* have understanding of local user data trends and measurement challenges in Hong Kong is essential.


 For interested parties, please submit your application with detailed CV on or before following date. Applicants are encouraged to submit their applications as soon as possible. The review of applications will continue until post is filled.




 03\-04\-2026




 Data collected will only be used for job application processing. Your data may be accessed by our appointed recruitment consultants who have agreed to keep confidence of all personal data in not less than the standards applicable to us. Applicants not being invited for interview within 4 weeks from the submission date may assume their applications unsuccessful.




 All related information will be kept up to 24 months and all personal data will be destroyed afterwards.




 For more information, please visit https://www.westk.hk or contact:




 Jane Lam /\+852 22002547

**Job Description**
 The LGT Capital Partners Private Equity Off\-Cycle Internship Program is a unique opportunity for top performing students to gain experience across the entire private equity investment process. The successful candidate would ideally start in
 **September/October 2026** 
 for
 **4 – 6 months** 
 either at our headquarters in Pfaeffikon (SZ) (close to Zurich) or in London. For high performers a progression to the Private Equity Analyst Program is a possibility.




 As an intern, you will join a team of experienced investment professionals fully dedicated to direct co\-investments. Since 2010, our team has committed more than USD 13 billion to over 400 direct co\-investments globally. Consideration of environmental, social and governance (ESG) issues is an integral part of our investment process as underlined by our dedicated impact fund focused on direct co\-investments.




 The Internship Will Provide You With Valuable Insights Into Our Business And Hands\-on Experience. Among Others, Interns Joining The Co\-Investment Team Will




* Assist the team in screening, analyzing, executing and monitoring direct co\-investment opportunities, including equity recaps and follow\-on financing;
* Perform financial analysis and modeling;
* Conduct industry research and business analysis;
* Support the preparation of investment committee materials;
* Maintain internal databases ensuring data quality and accuracy.


**Requirements**
* Outstanding academic credentials from a leading university and currently enrolled in a full\-time Bachelor or Master degree program in business, economics, finance or similar;
* Internship experience in a similar role is beneficial;
* Advanced Excel skills and a solid understanding of financial modeling;
* Excellent English writing and communication skills;
* Self\-starter personality with an international mindset;
* Strong analytical skills with focus on details and high degree of quality.


*Kindly note that visa sponsorship is not provided for this role.*
 Please upload your complete application documents: CV, motivation letter, diplomas, transcripts of your Bachelor and Master degree and your reference letters.




**Benefits**
* The LGT Sports club offers various activities such as a running club, outdoor workouts, and participation in sports events;
* A diverse culture full of mutual respect, teamwork and appreciation awaits you at LGT Capital Partners – as a global firm, LGT Capital Partners continues to evolve and expand the focus of our diversity, equity and inclusion trainings and initiatives;
* We‘re proud to be owned by the Princely family of Liechtenstein and our successful company is greatly inspired by their entrepreneurial attitude;
* Commitment to ESG since 2003: we believe that a long\-term approach, coupled with a strong focus on environmental, social and governance (ESG) principles, is essential to achieve sustained success. We seek to operate sustainably in our investments, as an employer, in the community and in our own operations.


**Contact Information**
 If you are interested in becoming an integral part of a successful alternative investment management team in an international, multicultural working environment we will be pleased to get to know you soon.




 For further information please contact us.




 Cassandra Fritschi




 Human Resources




 LGT Capital Partners AG, Pfaeffikon




**Contact**
 \+41 58 261 80 29

**Job summary/purpose:** 




 As a member of the Digital Customer Service team, the candidate shall support the team in providing excellent Customer Service, building exceptional clienteling relationship with to our customers, and drive sales business across Asia Pacific through different contact channels.










**Responsibilities:** 



* Supporting customers from various APAC countries with multi\-languages via various channels (Telephone, Livechat, Social Network, Email etc.);
* Motivate and coach team member to achieve sales and non\-sales objectives;
* Observe and review staff's performance with managers on regular basis;
* Build morale and foster team spirit, encourage open two\-way communication;
* Ensure the escalation processes are followed and successfully applied.
* Execute client outreach initiatives and drive sales through effective clienteling practices.
* Understands customers’ needs, preserve and resolve any service/product related issues;
* Provides assistance for customers during their E\-commerce purchase process and aftersales support;
* Communicate and liaise with internal parties to provide the most efficient method to solve customers’ issues;
* Follow\-through team's learning and practices, ensure on\-going applications at workplace;
* Assist the Digital Customer Service Manager with day to day operations to ensure the service levels and KPI targets are achieved, continually coach, mentor and motivate the team in always ensuring all client interactions are handled in line with brand values;















**Key Requirements:** 



* \+2 years of experience in Customer Service or have any fashion related qualification or experience
* Strong sales skills and clienteling experience
* Strong sense of initiative and solutions oriented with clear demonstration of a customer first mind\-set
* Fluent on both verbal and written skills in English, Mandarin and Cantonese
* Highly motivated, energetic and inspirational team leader
* Able to work collaboratively
* Excellent analytical and problem solving skills
* **Able to work in shifts and weekends/public holidays**









 Should you interested to this role, please apply through below:




 https://career5\.successfactors.eu/sfcareer/jobreqcareerpvt?jobId\=18706\&company\=pradaspaP2\&st\=2EB08468C5C61581677467F81FF71AB416B296C3

This position is divided into several specializations, including Acoustic Devices, Audio Algorithms, Healthcare Algorithms, Healthcare Electronics, Hearing Aids, and MEMS, etc. Please refer to the job descriptions and requirements based on the specific specialization.










**Base:** 
 Shenzhen/Hong Kong/Singapore










**Researcher (Healthcare Algorithm)** 




**Job Scope:** 




 1\. Lead algorithmic research for wearable devices, including physiological signal processing, analysis, feature extraction, and noise reduction, as well as edge AI research such as pattern recognition and large language model training.




 2\. Implement algorithms on hardware platforms to enhance functionality, performance, and reliability.




 3\. Apply algorithms to products to amplify their competitive edge and enhance user experiences.




**Job Requirement：** 




 1\. Ph.D., major in Signal \& Information Processing, Biomedical Engineering, Medical




 Information Engineering, Computer Science \& Technology, Software Engineering, Electronic Engineering, or related fields.




 3\. Possess clear logic, are adept at hypothesis formulation, and can swiftly track the latest global research findings to inspire innovation.




 4\. Passionate about research, driven to commercialize research outcomes globally, and find confidence, joy, and reward in doing so.




 5\. Experience in signal processing, mathematical modeling competitions, or biomedical projects is preferred.
















**Researcher (Healthcare Electronics)** 




**Job Scope:** 




 1\. Physiological signal processing, including chip selection and architecture design, gain and filtering solution design, embedded development, PCB design and testing;




 2\. Design of multiple circuit function modules and establishing the connection between the designed signals and the human body.




**Job Requirement:** 




 1\. PhD, majoring in electronic engineering,automation control, mechanical engineering, physics, or related fields, or have experience in electronics, sensors, and other projects with excellent academic performance and solid professional knowledge;




 2\. Proficient in using electronic design software with a good foundation in analog and digital circuits;




 3\. Have participated in electronic design competitions or other electronic competitions and won important awards, or have papers or patent achievements related to electronics or sensors, which will be preferred.
















**Researcher (Audio Algorithm)** 




**Job Scope:** 




 1\.Responsible for the research of algorithms applied to acoustic devices and hearing aids, such as front\-end processing and sound effects, voice enhancement, active noise reduction, auditory scene analysis and other acoustic and audiological algorithms;




 2\.Responsible for the implementation of the algorithms on the hardware platform to improve the function, performance and reliability of the algorithms;




 3\.Responsible for the application of algorithms in products to enhance product advantages and user experience.




**Job Requirement：** 




 1\. PhD, majoring in acoustics, audiology, electronic engineer, signal processing and related fields;




 2\. Clear logic, good at conjecture, able to quickly track the latest global scientific research results, and inspire innovation;




 3\. Loving scientific research, committed to the marketization of scientific research results, and gain confidence, fun and profit from it;




 4\.Experience in signal processing, mathematical modeling competitions, acoustics projects is preferred.
















**Researcher (Acoustic Devices)** 




**Job Scope:** 




 1\. Carry out research on acoustic devices and acoustic systems, and pre\-research the core acoustic technology of products;




 2\. Participate in the development of the product, responsible for the development of the acoustic part of the content.




**Job Requirement:** 




 1\. PhD, majoring in acoustics, mechanics, mechanical engineer, electronics, automation,etc.,




 or have experience in acoustics, vibration, sensors and other projects;




 2\. Focused, like to explore the essence of things, and pursue excellence in technology;




 3\. Clear logic, good at guessing, able to quickly track the latest global scientific research results, and inspire innovation;




 4\. Love scientific research, hope to quickly apply the research results to products, marketing the world, and gain confidence, fun and profit from talented people;




 5\. Experience in acoustics, sensors, transducers and other related projects is preferred.
















**Researcher (Hearing Aids)** 




**Job Scope:** 




 1\.Use speech signal processing, acoustic device innovation and other weapons to solve hearing compensation, intelligibility improvement, sound quality optimization and other challenges;




 2\.Become a conqueror for fundamental technology, algorithm architect, and even industry




 standard setter;




 3\.Collaborate with multi\-disciplinary teams to explore the frontiers of cross\-disciplines.




**Job Requirement:** 




 1\. PhD, majoring in Computer and Information Engineering, Acoustics, Audiology or Biomedical Engineering, Electronics and Automation, Artificial Intelligence;




 2\. Experience in speech signal processing, embedded, audiology related projects and topics is preferred;




 3\. A sense of mission and responsibility to improve the quality of life of the hearing impaired;




 4\. Excellent scientific research ability, focused and curious, with strong self\-driven and learning ability, able to quickly familiarize and master new fields, and pursue excellence and creativity.

Originating in 1964, CIGP has been providing independent and expert financial advice to business owners, high net worth individuals and family offices globally.












 With an entrepreneurial spirit which has created continuous business growth, CIGP is looking for an experienced Middle Office Analyst/Associate.












 If you are a creative, adaptable, self\-driven and passionate individual who is up for a challenge and keen to make an impact, please submit your application today.












 To learn more about CIGP, please visit 

 www.cigp.com

 .





  




**Roles and Responsibilities** 





 You will take up the important role of Middle Office Analyst/Associate and will be responsible as such for duties including but not limited to:




* Develop a good understanding of CIGP’s operational workflow and execute the daily Operations tasks together with the team;
* Book trades, corporate actions and other transactions in our Portfolio Management System (“PMS”);
* Maintain daily Marked\-to\-Market valuations within our PMS;
* Instruct trade settlements with our various custodian banks;
* Communicate and work hand\-in\-hand with external financial counterparties (e.g. brokers, custodians) in order to ensure a successful and smooth trade settlement flow;
* Perform daily cash and securities positions reconciliations, between the clients’ accounts and the banks’ cash \& securities statements, as well as monthly securities reconciliations;
* Send out trade confirmations and statements to CIGP’s clients via our proprietary system, as well as prepare corporate action notes;
* Produce various reports on a weekly/monthly/quarterly basis, as required;
* Monitor CIGP’s exposure to its financial counterparties;
* Communicate daily with the Front Office team, in order to answer ad\-hoc request(s) and solve potential issue(s) on the spot; and
* Work closely with our overseas offices (e.g. Geneva) on various projects, as required.









 Additional responsibilities and job evolution:



* Open new Brokerage and Custody relationships and markets, as and when required by the business; and
* Actively participate in the improvement and optimization of the trading execution, booking and settlement process.









**Requirements** 



* You have 3 years or more of experience within the Middle or Back Office of a financial institution (both profiles will be considered);
* You are proficient in Microsoft Office (Excel, Word and Power Point) – an advanced level in Excel modelling, such as VBA, is a plus;
* You are persistent and able to work with a positive problem solving mind\-set;
* You are a quick learner with the curiosity to understand how things work, possessing strong attention to details and able to work independently under tight deadlines;
* You are fluent in English (proficiency in other languages is a plus);
* An international background (worked and/or studied abroad) shall be favoured; and
* Less experienced candidates will be considered as Middle Office Analyst.









*We are an equal opportunity employer and welcome applications from all qualified candidates. Every application will be treated in the strictest confidence. Personal data provided will be used for recruitment purposes only.* 




*Applicants who are not invited for interview within 10 weeks may consider their applications unsuccessful. Personal data of unsuccessful applicant will be destroyed within 12 months.* 




*Under the Personal Data (Privacy) Ordinance, you may request access to, and/or correction of your personal data in relation to your application. If you wish to do so, kindly reach out to us by email.*
